[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2669561685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102934#issuecomment-2669561685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102934","id":2669561685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fHkdV","user":{"login":"lighttroupe","id":1422772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjI3NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1422772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe","html_url":"https://github.com/lighttroupe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T19:25:14Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T19:26:55Z","body":"GOOD: This is an O(1) operation to save an O(n) operation.\nBAD: The \"approx equal\" test adds a cost, and for nodes without children there's no benefit.\n\nIdeally a node could say...\n\n> if (subtree node count > X and new_value.approx_equal(current_value)) return\n\n...as that would only add one integer compare to the worst case, but I don't know if Godot nodes keep a cached count of subtree nodes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2669561685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2669582583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102934#issuecomment-2669582583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102934","id":2669582583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fHpj3","user":{"login":"lighttroupe","id":1422772,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjI3NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1422772?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe","html_url":"https://github.com/lighttroupe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lighttroupe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T19:36:00Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T19:36:00Z","body":"If there's no cached count of subtree nodes, using the direct child count would at least avoid work for what I imagine is the most common case eg setting position on a node with zero children.\n\n> // avoid subtree update work if setting to existing value\n> // avoid approx_equal work for common case of no children\n> if (child count > 0 and new_value.approx_equal(current_value)) return \n\nI'm not sure how we could profile this sort of thing, as it totally depends on how a project uses nodes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot